 "notes": [
  "Source PDF mirrors the 1st Constituent Assembly PDF's layout: an original members list under section headings 'EAST BENGAL-40', 'PUNJAB', 'NORTH-WEST FRONTIER PROVICE-4' [sic, PDF typo for PROVINCE], 'SINDH-5', 'BALUCHISTAN-1', 'KARCHI-1' [sic, PDF typo for KARACHI]; followed by a changes list headed (verbatim, apparently carried over/mislabeled from the 1st Assembly file) 'CHANGES MEMBERS FIRST CONSTITUTE ASSEMBLY FROM AUGUST, 1955-1958', which in context documents 2nd Constituent Assembly membership changes.",
  "Only an S.No and address column are given; no seat/constituency code and no party column, so seat and raw_constituency are null for original-list members. For changes-list entries, the address/place given is kept in raw_constituency; province is left null since no province heading groups these entries.",
  "Karachi's 1 member is recorded with province 'Sindh' (Karachi is not a listed schema province) with a remark noting the PDF's own separate 'KARACHI-1' heading.",
  "Original-list total transcribed: 72 members (East Bengal 40, Punjab 21, NWFP 4, Sindh 5, Baluchistan 1, Karachi 1) - all entries under each heading had printed names, no numbering gaps found.",
  "'Changes' list total transcribed: 18 members (one 'JUNE, 1956' batch is marked 'NIL' and yields no member).",
  "As with the 1st Constituent Assembly, members were elected indirectly by provincial legislatures; elected_via is 'indirect' for the original list and 'by_election' for the changes-list entries.",
  "No reserved women's or minority/non-Muslim seat heading appears anywhere in this PDF; all entries recorded as seat_type 'general'.",
  "OCR text had scattered stray spaces inside words; these were collapsed to normal spelling without otherwise altering names.",
  "Total members recorded for Assembly 2: 90 (72 original + 18 from the changes list)."
 ],
